// The branch predictor (Ref docs: the timing model's Branch prediction):
// a 256-entry BTB, direct mapped by the low 8 bits of the bundle's PC and
// tagged with the rest, shared by all threads. An entry predicts its
// target while its 2-bit counter is below 3 (0 strongly taken). Only
// mispredicts train it: a taken one creates an entry at 0 (or lowers the
// counter and sets the target), a not-taken one raises the counter (or
// creates an entry at 3). MISPREDICTS is checked on the timing model.
//
// An inner loop (4 passes) run 5 times by an outer loop. The inner
// branch's counter: instance 1 mispredicts at entry (creates the entry at
// 0) and exit (-> 1); instances 2 and 3 only at exit (-> 2, -> 3). From
// then on the counter starts each instance at 3, "not taken", so
// instances 4 and 5 mispredict at entry (-> 2) and exit (-> 3) again:
// 2+1+1+2+2 = 8. The outer branch: 2. In all 10: the correctly predicted
// taken passes never pull the counter back toward "taken".

    || + $r1 ($i64) $r0 4 ;                 // the outer loop: 5 passes
outer:
    || + $r2 ($i64) $r0 3 ;                 // the inner loop: 4 passes
inner:
    || + $r3 ($i64) $r3 1 ;
    || ? ($i64) $r2 > --1 $goto inner ;
    || ? ($i64) $r1 > --1 $goto outer ;
    || $halt ;
